["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The wrong shell in the right gun can burst a barrel. Two numbers prevent it: gauge and chamber length.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bore sizes to scale: 12 gauge 18.5 mm, 16 gauge 16.8 mm, 20 gauge 15.6 mm, 28 gauge 14.0 mm, .410 bore 10.4 mm. A smaller gauge number means a bigger bore.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Gauge: bore to scale</text>\n<g data-tip=\"12 gauge|Bore about 18.5 mm.\" data-tip-dot=\"52,130\"><circle cx=\"51.6\" cy=\"130\" r=\"29.6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"51.6\" y=\"185.6\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text x=\"51.6\" y=\"205.6\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18.5 mm</text>\n<g data-tip=\"16 gauge|Bore about 16.8 mm.\" data-tip-dot=\"134,130\"><circle cx=\"134.1\" cy=\"130\" r=\"26.9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"134.1\" y=\"182.9\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">16</text>\n<text x=\"134.1\" y=\"202.9\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">16.8 mm</text>\n<g data-tip=\"20 gauge|Bore about 15.6 mm.\" data-tip-dot=\"212,130\"><circle cx=\"211.9\" cy=\"130\" r=\"25.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"211.9\" y=\"181.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20</text>\n<text x=\"211.9\" y=\"201.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15.6 mm</text>\n<g data-tip=\"28 gauge|Bore about 14.0 mm.\" data-tip-dot=\"285,130\"><circle cx=\"285.3\" cy=\"130\" r=\"22.4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"285.3\" y=\"178.4\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">28</text>\n<text x=\"285.3\" y=\"198.4\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14.0 mm</text>\n<g data-tip=\".410 bore|Bore about 10.4 mm.\" data-tip-dot=\"350,130\"><circle cx=\"350.3\" cy=\"130\" r=\"16.6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></g>\n<text x=\"350.3\" y=\"172.6\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">.410</text>\n<text x=\"350.3\" y=\"192.6\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10.4 mm</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"280.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bigger number, smaller bore.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Gauge: smaller number, bigger bore <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>12 gauge has the widest choice of steel duck loads <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: gauge in full</summary><ul><li>Gauge is an old measure: the number of lead balls of bore size that make one pound. So 12 gauge is bigger than 20 (70%, Wikipedia, gauge).</li><li>Nominal bores: 12 gauge 18.5 mm (.729 in), 16 gauge 16.8 mm, 20 gauge 15.6 mm (.615 in), 28 gauge 14.0 mm (70%, Wikipedia, gauge). The .410 bore is 0.410 in, about 10.4 mm (arithmetic).</li><li>.410 is a bore size in inches, not a gauge <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>20 gauge kicks less but its steel duck loads are weaker (65%, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-guide/3\">Choosing your shotgun</a>).</li><li>Migratory birds: no shotgun bigger than 10 gauge (99%, s. 37(1)(c), <a href=\"#/s/rb-migratory-birds/32\">Rule Book</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Chamber length and shell length. A 3 inch chamber takes 2 3/4 inch (70 mm) and 3 inch (76 mm) shells. A 3 1/2 inch (89 mm) shell is too long for it and must never be loaded. The length on the box is the fired length.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Chamber: shell must fit</text>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"70\" width=\"300\" height=\"56\" fill=\"#3b4045\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"80\" width=\"236\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#cfd5d8\"/>\n<path d=\"M276 80 L300 86 L300 110 L276 116 Z\" fill=\"#cfd5d8\"/>\n<rect x=\"300\" y=\"86\" width=\"40\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#cfd5d8\"/>\n<line x1=\"158.0\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"158.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"158.0\" cy=\"80.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"72.2\" y=\"47.0\" width=\"175.7\" height=\"23.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"160.0\" y=\"64.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3 in chamber (76 mm)</text>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"158\" width=\"217\" height=\"24\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3b6e8f\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"157\" width=\"14\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/>\n<text x=\"60.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 3/4 in (70 mm)</text>\n<path d=\"M354 170 L361.3 177.7 L376 161.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"198\" width=\"236\" height=\"24\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3b6e8f\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"197\" width=\"14\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/>\n<text x=\"60.0\" y=\"216.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 in (76 mm)</text>\n<path d=\"M354 210 L361.3 217.7 L376 201.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"238\" width=\"276\" height=\"24\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3b6e8f\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"237\" width=\"14\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/>\n<text x=\"60.0\" y=\"256.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 1/2 in (89 mm)</text>\n<line x1=\"355\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"355\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<line x1=\"276\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"276\" y2=\"272\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"292.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never longer than the barrel stamp.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A 3 in chamber fires 2 3/4 in and 3 in shells <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Never a shell longer than the barrel stamp <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: chamber in full</summary><ul><li>The length on the box is the fired length; the crimp unfolds into the cone ahead of the chamber <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Beretta: the A300 Outlander shoots 70 mm (2 3/4 in) to 76 mm (3 in) shells without adjustment (95%, A300 manual).</li><li>Remington: \"NEVER USE AMMUNITION WHICH EXCEEDS THE CHAMBER LENGTH SHOWN ON THE BARREL\" (95%, 870 manual).</li><li>3 1/2 in chambers add recoil and cost for little gain on ducks (65%, <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-guide/3\">Choosing your shotgun</a>).</li><li>My lean: a 3 in chamber. It covers every duck, goose and grouse load you need (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read the barrel stamp before you load: gauge, chamber length and, on some guns, a steel shot proof mark. Then read the shell box and match both.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Read the stamp, match the box</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"70\" width=\"360\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#3b4045\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"99.0\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e9ecee\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 GA   3 in   CHAMBER</text>\n<line x1=\"200.0\" y1=\"66.0\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"72.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"72.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"118.1\" y=\"42.0\" width=\"163.8\" height=\"24.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"60.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 the barrel stamp</text>\n<rect x=\"80\" y=\"150\" width=\"240\" height=\"90\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"176.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 GA   2 3/4 in</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">STEEL  No. 2  1 1/8 oz</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"224.0\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1450 fps</text>\n<line x1=\"200.0\" y1=\"148.0\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"152.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"152.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"136.5\" y=\"124.0\" width=\"127.1\" height=\"24.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"142.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2 the shell box</text>\n<path d=\"M336 196 L345.3 205.8 L364 184.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"286.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Same gauge. Shell no longer than the chamber.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>1: the barrel stamp. 2: the box. Same gauge, shell no longer <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Check every box, every time, even \"the usual\" (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where the marks are</summary><ul><li>Beretta: the gauge and chamber markings are on the side of the barrel (95%, A300 manual).</li><li>Remington: \"BEFORE LOADING, ALWAYS CHECK THE BARREL MARKING FOR THE CORRECT GAUGE AND CHAMBER LENGTH\" (95%, 870 manual).</li><li>The shell head is stamped with its gauge too (95%, 870 manual, Picture B).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The 12 20 burst: a 20 gauge shell dropped into a 12 gauge gun can slide down the barrel and stick. A 12 gauge shell loaded behind it fires into the blocked barrel and can burst it. Keep 20 gauge shells out of your 12 gauge kit.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"20\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Wrong gauge: the 12 20 burst</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"110\" width=\"360\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#3b4045\"/>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"116\" width=\"360\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#cfd5d8\"/>\n<rect x=\"190\" y=\"118\" width=\"60\" height=\"24\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#d4b21f\" stroke=\"#17201A\"/>\n<rect x=\"190\" y=\"117\" width=\"10\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/>\n<rect x=\"24\" y=\"117\" width=\"74\" height=\"26\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#3b6e8f\" stroke=\"#17201A\"/>\n<rect x=\"24\" y=\"116\" width=\"12\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#c9a227\"/>\n<line x1=\"220.0\" y1=\"102.0\" x2=\"220.0\" y2=\"118.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"220.0\" cy=\"118.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"151.7\" y=\"79.0\" width=\"136.6\" height=\"23.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"220.0\" y=\"96.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20 ga shell stuck</text>\n<line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"174.0\" x2=\"60.0\" y2=\"144.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"144.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"-0.4\" y=\"173.0\" width=\"140.8\" height=\"23.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"190.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 ga shell behind</text>\n<circle cx=\"252\" cy=\"130\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" opacity=\"0.35\"/>\n<circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"232\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"237.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n<text x=\"46.0\" y=\"237.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Keep 20 ga shells out of the 12 ga bag</text>\n<circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"262\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"267.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n<text x=\"46.0\" y=\"267.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weak shot or odd sound: stop, unload, check bore</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"292.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">From the Remington 870 manual.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A 20 gauge shell can drop into a 12 gauge barrel and stick <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>A 12 loaded behind it can burst the barrel <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the manual's warning</summary><ul><li>Remington calls this \"a 12/20 burst, and it can kill you\" (95%, 870 manual).</li><li>20 gauge shells are often yellow, but colour is not a rule (Tip, 60%). Read the head stamp.</li><li>\"If the noise or recoil of your firearm seems weak, stop everything, unload your firearm and be sure nothing is lodged in the barrel\" (95%, 870 manual).</li><li>Keep one gauge per bag, per pocket, per boat (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): One gun, one gauge, one bag. Mixing is how barrels split.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Grabbing a friend's 20 gauge shells \"just for today\".</li><li>Buying 3 1/2 in shells for a 3 in gun because they were on sale.</li><li>Reading the price on the box and not the length.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>When you buy the gun, read the stamp out loud with the clerk, and write it on a label inside your shell bag.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Maker manuals read directly <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Bore sizes from a secondary source <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.rem870.com/remington_model_870_manual.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Remington Model 870 instruction book, form RD 7058</a>: barrel marking, 12/20 burst. Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://berettaweb.com/Munuals/Beretta%20Owner%20Manual%20A300%20Outlander%20LD.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beretta A300 Outlander instruction manual, 09/2011</a>: chamber and shell lengths. Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gauge_(firearms\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikipedia: gauge (firearms)</a>): nominal bore sizes. Checked 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Migratory Birds Regulations, 2022, s. 37(1)(c), via the app Rule Book <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul></details>"]